    {
      "severity": "MINOR",
      "area": "Migration / tenant deletion",
      "file": "prisma/migrations/20261016190000_project_line_accounts/migration.sql",
      "issue": "The new foreign keys to LineOfficialAccount use ON DELETE RESTRICT, which Postgres checks immediately even while a Vendor cascade is still deleting the referencing rows.",
      "impact": "Deleting a vendor that has projects, identities, login states or drafts can fail, depending on the order in which the cascades run.",
      "evidence": "SalesProject, LineUserIdentity, LineLoginState and LineRichMenuDraft each reference LineOfficialAccount with ON DELETE RESTRICT, and all of them also cascade from Vendor.",
      "recommended_fix": "Use onDelete: NoAction (ON DELETE NO ACTION) so the check runs at the end of the statement, after the vendor cascade finishes, while still blocking direct account deletion.",
      "required_test": "Delete a Vendor that has two accounts, linked projects, identities, deliveries, login states and drafts, and assert it succeeds.",
